@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.779 = private unnamed_addr constant [642 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function calls with parameters that indicate the use of insecure\0ASSL and TLS protocol versions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASeveral highly publicized exploitable flaws have been discovered in all\0Aversions of SSL and early versions of TLS. The following versions are\0Aconsidered insecure, and should be avoided:\0A- SSL v2\0A- SSL v3\0A- TLS v1\0A- TLS v1.1\0A\0AThis method supports detection on the Python's built-in `ssl` module and\0Athe `pyOpenSSL` module.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport ssl\0A\0Assl.wrap_socket(ssl_version=ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport ssl\0A\0Assl.wrap_socket(ssl_version=ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2)\0A```\0A", align 1
