@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.800 = private unnamed_addr constant [878 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for boolean positional arguments in function calls.\0A\0ASome functions are whitelisted by default. To extend the list of allowed calls\0Aconfigure the [`lint.flake8-boolean-trap.extend-allowed-calls`] option.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ACalling a function with boolean positional arguments is confusing as the\0Ameaning of the boolean value is not clear to the caller, and to future\0Areaders of the code.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Adef func(flag: bool) -> None: ...\0A\0A\0Afunc(True)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef func(flag: bool) -> None: ...\0A\0A\0Afunc(flag=True)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-boolean-trap.extend-allowed-calls`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Calls](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#calls)\0A- [_How to Avoid \E2\80\9CThe Boolean Trap\E2\80\9D_ by Adam Johnson](https://adamj.eu/tech/2021/07/10/python-type-hints-how-to-avoid-the-boolean-trap/)\0A", align 1
