@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.804 = private unnamed_addr constant [582 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `assertRaises` and `pytest.raises` context managers that catch\0A`Exception` or `BaseException`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThese forms catch every `Exception`, which can lead to tests passing even\0Aif, e.g., the code under consideration raises a `SyntaxError` or\0A`IndentationError`.\0A\0AEither assert for a more specific exception (builtin or custom), or use\0A`assertRaisesRegex` or `pytest.raises(..., match=<REGEX>)` respectively.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aself.assertRaises(Exception, foo)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aself.assertRaises(SomeSpecificException, foo)\0A```\0A", align 1
