@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.829 = private unnamed_addr constant [566 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for exception handlers that catch non-exception classes.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ACatching classes that do not inherit from `BaseException` will raise a\0A`TypeError`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    1 / 0\0Aexcept 1:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    1 / 0\0Aexcept ZeroDivisionError:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `except` clause](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#except-clause)\0A- [Python documentation: Built-in Exceptions](https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#built-in-exceptions)\0A", align 1
