@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.834 = private unnamed_addr constant [997 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `break`, `continue`, and `return` statements in `finally`\0Ablocks.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe use of `break`, `continue`, and `return` statements in `finally` blocks\0Acan cause exceptions to be silenced.\0A\0A`finally` blocks execute regardless of whether an exception is raised. If a\0A`break`, `continue`, or `return` statement is reached in a `finally` block,\0Aany exception raised in the `try` or `except` blocks will be silenced.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef speed(distance, time):\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError:\0A        raise ValueError(\22Time cannot be zero\22)\0A    finally:\0A        return 299792458  # `ValueError` is silenced\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef speed(distance, time):\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError:\0A        raise ValueError(\22Time cannot be zero\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `try` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#the-try-statement)\0A", align 1
