@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.895 = private unnamed_addr constant [544 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for member imports that should instead be accessed by importing the\0Amodule.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AConsistency is good. Use a common convention for imports to make your code\0Amore readable and idiomatic.\0A\0AFor example, it's common to import `pandas` as `pd`, and then access\0Amembers like `Series` via `pd.Series`, rather than importing `Series`\0Adirectly.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom pandas import Series\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Apd.Series\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-import-conventions.banned-from`\0A", align 1
