@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.997 = private unnamed_addr constant [466 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for assignments to the variable `df`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAlthough `df` is a common variable name for a Pandas `DataFrame`, it's not a\0Agreat variable name for production code, as it's non-descriptive and\0Aprone to name conflicts.\0A\0AInstead, use a more descriptive variable name.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Adf = pd.read_csv(\22animals.csv\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Aanimals = pd.read_csv(\22animals.csv\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
