@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1005 = private unnamed_addr constant [1622 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for class methods that use a name other than `cls` for their\0Afirst argument.\0A\0AThe method `__new__` is exempted from this\0Acheck and the corresponding violation is caught by\0A[`bad-staticmethod-argument`][PLW0211].\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends the use of `cls` as the first argument for all class\0Amethods:\0A\0A> Always use `cls` for the first argument to class methods.\0A>\0A> If a function argument\E2\80\99s name clashes with a reserved keyword, it is generally better to\0A> append a single trailing underscore rather than use an abbreviation or spelling corruption.\0A> Thus `class_` is better than `clss`. (Perhaps better is to avoid such clashes by using a synonym.)\0A\0ANames can be excluded from this rule using the [`lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`]\0Aor [`lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`] configuration options. For example,\0Ato allow the use of `klass` as the first argument to class methods, set\0Athe [`lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`] option to `[\22klass\22]`.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Example:\0A    @classmethod\0A    def function(self, data): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Example:\0A    @classmethod\0A    def function(cls, data): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as renaming a method parameter\0Acan change the behavior of the program.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.classmethod-decorators`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.staticmethod-decorators`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#function-and-method-arguments\0A[PLW0211]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/bad-staticmethod-argument/\0A", align 1
