@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1062 = private unnamed_addr constant [458 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for iteration over a `set` literal where each element in the set is\0Aitself a literal value.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIterating over a `set` is less efficient than iterating over a sequence\0Atype, like `list` or `tuple`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afor number in {1, 2, 3}:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afor number in (1, 2, 3):\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `set`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#set)\0A", align 1
