@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1191 = private unnamed_addr constant [928 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for membership tests against single-item containers.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APerforming a membership test against a container (like a `list` or `set`)\0Awith a single item is less readable and less efficient than comparing\0Aagainst the item directly.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A1 in [1]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A1 == 1\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AWhen the right-hand side is a string, the fix is marked as unsafe.\0AThis is because `c in \22a\22` is true both when `c` is `\22a\22` and when `c` is the empty string,\0Aso the fix can change the behavior of your program in these cases.\0A\0AAdditionally, if there are comments within the fix's range,\0Ait will also be marked as unsafe.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Comparisons](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#comparisons)\0A- [Python documentation: Membership test operations](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#membership-test-operations)\0A", align 1
