@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1229 = private unnamed_addr constant [570 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for usages of `collections.deque` that have an empty iterable as the first argument.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to use an empty literal as a deque's iterable, since this is already the default behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom collections import deque\0A\0Aqueue = deque(set())\0Aqueue = deque([], 10)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom collections import deque\0A\0Aqueue = deque()\0Aqueue = deque(maxlen=10)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `collections.deque`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.html#collections.deque)\0A", align 1
@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1230 = private unnamed_addr constant [46 x i8] c"Unnecessary empty iterable within a deque call", align 1
